# Third-Party Licenses

`searchlight_cli` statically links a number of third-party Rust crates (including the bundled
SQLite and DuckDB engines). Their licenses — MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, and other permissive terms —
require the license text and copyright notice to be preserved and distributed alongside the
software. This file exists to satisfy that requirement: it lists every dependency compiled into
the binary, its license, and the full text of each license.

This file is generated by [`cargo-about`](https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-about) from
`Cargo.lock` and `about.toml`. To regenerate it after a dependency change, run from the project
root:

```
cargo about generate about.hbs -o THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md
```

